# Everything in here is generated by DMS -- cursor.kdl included, despite
# looking hand written; it carries the same "DO NOT EDIT" banner as the rest
# and follows cursorSettings in dank/settings.json.
#
# What decides whether a fragment is worth tracking is not who writes it but
# whether anything else could put it back:
#
#   binds.kdl, windowrules.kdl   tracked, and the important ones. There are no
#                                keybinds anywhere in dank/settings.json, so
#                                binds.kdl is the only record of the keymap --
#                                including hand-tuned entries like
#                                `Mod+T { spawn "alacritty"; }`. Losing it
#                                loses the bindings for good.
#   alttab, layout, wpblur,      tracked, but cheaply reconstructable: DMS
#   cursor, input                rewrites them from dank/settings.json, which
#                                is tracked, so they are convenience not
#                                insurance.
#   colors.kdl, outputs.kdl      ignored, below. colors is matugen's output
#                                for the current wallpaper and theme, and
#                                outputs is regenerated from whichever display
#                                profile is active -- so it flips on every dock
#                                and undock, and committing it only records
#                                which desk someone was sitting at.
#                                dank/monitors.json holds the profiles.
#
# Safe to leave absent: every include in niri/config.kdl is `optional=true`, so
# a fresh checkout warns rather than failing, and DMS rewrites both within
# moments of starting. config.kdl does set border colours of its own, though
# not focus-ring or tab-indicator, so the very first frames use niri's defaults
# rather than the theme.
colors.kdl
outputs.kdl
